<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Ardalan</h1><p class="st-meta">1300 CE – 1867 CE (approx.) · capital Sanandaj</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kurdish principality in western Iran that ruled for more than five centuries and made Sanandaj a centre of Kurdish literature.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ardalan family traced its descent to a semi-legendary Baba Ardalan and emerged as rulers of the Kurdish lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrizor">Sharazur</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> by the 14th century. The principality lay on the frontier between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, and the Ardalans shifted between them before settling mostly under Iranian overlordship.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ardalan walis ruled a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Kurdish population of farmers and tribes, sending troops and tribute to the shahs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soleyman-khan-ardalan">Soleyman Khan Ardalan</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanandaj">Sanandaj</a> (Sinneh) in the 1630s as his capital. The court patronised poetry in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorani-language">Gorani</a>, the literary Kurdish of the region, and in the 19th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastoureh-ardalan">Mastoureh Ardalan</a> wrote a history of the dynasty, one of the first by a Kurdish woman. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amanullah-khan">Amanullah Khan</a> built palaces and gardens in Sanandaj.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran</a> steadily reduced Ardalan autonomy, and in 1867 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naser-al-din-shah-qajar">Naser al-Din Shah</a> replaced the last wali with a royal governor, ending the principality.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ardalan.jpg" alt="Ardalan" width="320" height="208"><figcaption>Image: George F. Cram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cram%27s_Family_Atlas_(Ardalan).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1300 CE – 1867 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sanandaj</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Soleyman Khan Ardalan, Amanullah Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kurdish (Gorani)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Iran, Iraq</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Ardalan, Ardalan principality</dd></dl></aside></div>
